  "question": {
    "text": "A fighter plane, flying horizontally with a speed $360 \\mathrm{kmph}$ at an altitude of $500 \\mathrm{~m}$ drops a bomb for a target straight ahead of it on the ground. The bomb .should be dropped at what approximate distance ahead of the target ? Assume that acceleration due to gravity $(\\mathrm{g})$ is $10 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-2}$. Also neglect air drag"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$1000 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$50 \\sqrt{5} \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$500 \\sqrt{5} \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$866 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: \r\n$v=360 \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h}=100 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s} .$\r\n$\\mathrm{h}=500 \\mathrm{~m}$\r\n$\\mathrm{R}=\\mathrm{u} \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\mathrm{~h}}{\\mathrm{~g}}}=100 \\times \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\times 500}{10}}=1000 \\mathrm{~m}$"
  }
}